    "source_file": "azo_yellow.md",
    "content": "While it may _look_ like a brown, this is a tremendous saturated yellow with depth which expands the gamut. It is incredibly useful- maybe almost indispensable for increasing the range of hues in oil paint and also for depicting lower-lightness high-chroma yellows.\nAs many painters will tell you, it can be difficult to descent down into the lower lightness steps of yellows. One may start out thinking it's as easy dancing the Grapevine step only to find out it's more like a Viennese Waltz. PY150 is a color that can help maintain high chroma in difficult mixes.\nhttps://paintlist.com/pigment-notebook/py150"
